    "created_at": "2025-11-20T18:36:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-21T18:31:32Z",
    "body": "Okay, I've looked at that [section](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-address-element). I now understand the (oddly?) constrained usage for `address`, as defined. But why does it say:\n> (The [p](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-p-element) element is the appropriate element for marking up postal addresses in general.)\n\nIn what way is the `p` element a more appropriate element for an address than a `div`? What forms the (linguistic) semantic argument that an address is a paragraph?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
